 {:race/name        "Dark Elves"
  :race/description "In the language of Aman all Elves that did not cross the Great Sea were Dark Elves, and the term is sometimes used thus, 94, 102; when Caranthir called Thingol a Dark Elf it was intended opprobriously, and was especially so, since Thingol had been to Aman and was not accounted among them (46). But in the period of the Exile of the Noldor it was often used of the Elves of Middle-earth other than the Noldor and the Sindar, and is then virtually equivalent to Avari (94, 114, 132). Different again is the title Dark Elf of the Sindarin Elf Eöl, 124, 126, 192; but at 128 Turgon no doubt meant that Eöl was a Dark Elf in the first sense."
  :race/page        [42 46 81 94 98 102 114 124 126 128 132 192]
  :race/appears-in  [[:chapter/name "Of the Coming of the Elves and the Captivity of Melkor"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Thingol and Melian"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Sindar"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Men"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Return of the Noldor"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Beleriand and its Realms"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Maeglin"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of the Coming of Men into the West"]
                     [:chapter/name "Of Túrin Turambar"]]}

